          #AdamsQuillenTheorem.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} stable homotopy groups of spheres
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(\mathbb{S})
              are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of the (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"}> cyclic
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} im(J|_{SO})
              of the J-homomorphism, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#JHom"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+group"} special orthogonal group
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+e-invariant"} Adams e-invariant
            %p Moreover,
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi mod
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0 \;mod \;8
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi mod
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1 \;mod \; 8
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  positive the J-homomorphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝕊
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(J) \colon \pi_n(S O) \to \pi_n(\mathbb{S})
                  is
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injective
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 3
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi mod
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 3\; mod\; 8
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 7
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi mod
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 7 \; mod \; 8
                  hence for
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo =
                          %mn 4
                          %mi k
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 4 k -1
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order+of+a+group"} order
                  of the image is equal to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/denominator"} denominator
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi B
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 4
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_{2k}/4k
                  in its reduced form, where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi B
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_{2k}
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernoulli+number"} Bernoulli number
              %li
                %p for all other cases the image is necessarily zero.
          %p
            This characterization of the image of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Adams66"}> Adams 66
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Quillen71"} Quillen 71
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Sullivan74"} Sullivan 74
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J(\pi_{4n-1}(S O))
            is (
            %a{:href => "#Adams65a"} Adams 65a, theorem 3.7
            and the direct summand property is (
            %a{:href => "#Adams66"}> Adams 66, theorems 1.1-1.6.
            ). That the image is a direct summand of the codomain is proven for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#Switzer75"}> Switzer 75, end of chapter 19
            ).
          %p
            A modern version of the proof, using methods from
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+homotopy+theory"} chromatic homotopy theory
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Lorman13"} Lorman 13
          %p
            The statement of the theorem is recalled for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#RavenelCh1"}> Ravenel, chapter 1, theorem 1.1.13
            ). Another computation of the image of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            is in (
            %a{:href => "#RavenelChapter5"}> Ravenel, chapter 5, section 3
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_7 Remark
            %p
              The order of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
